.TH SIG_POP 3
.SH NAME
sig_pop \- pop a signal handler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "sig.h"
.PP
.BI "int sig_pop(int " sig ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sig_pop
undoes the most recent
.BR sig_push (3)
or
.BR sig_pusha (3)
for the signal
.IR sig ,
restoring the handler that was active before it via the internal
per-signal handler stack. This function is MT-unsafe.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of handlers remaining on the stack for
.I sig
on success, or -1 on failure, with
.I errno
set to
.B EINVAL
if
.I sig
is not a valid signal number,
.B EFAULT
if the stack for
.I sig
is empty, or an error from
.BR sig_action (3)
if restoring the previous handler fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sig_push (3)
